            <abstract xml:lang="de"><p resp="#regest">Bürgermeister und Rat zu St. Gallen erinnern an ihr Schreiben vom 3. Juni 1645 betreffend den Nachlass des verstorbenen Glasmachers Melchior Wüldin. Da die Erben des Caspar Schlumpf den Arrest gegen den Nachlass aufheben, bitten die St. Galler Behörden Amsterdam, den Nachlass an St. Gallen abzuliefern. Wüldin sei bis zu seinem Tod St. Galler Bürger gewesen, sein Sohn sei der rechtmässige Erbe, weshalb die Erbschaft in St. Gallen zu entscheiden sei.</p></abstract>
            <abstract xml:lang="en" resp="#mt"><p>Burgomaster and Council of St. Gallen refer to their letter of 3 June 1645 concerning the estate of the deceased glassmaker Melchior Wüldin. Since the heirs of Caspar Schlumpf lift the arrest against the estate, the St. Gallen authorities ask Amsterdam to deliver the estate to St. Gallen. Wüldin had been a citizen of St. Gallen until his death, his son is the lawful heir, which is why the inheritance is to be decided in St. Gallen.</p></abstract>
